# Spec-Driven Development (SDD) Requirements
## Hiking Trip Planning & Community Webpage

**Document purpose:** This document defines the functional and non-functional specifications for the hiking webpage prior to implementation. Each requirement is written to be testable and unambiguous, per SDD practice — implementation should be traceable back to a specific requirement ID.

---

## 1. Scope

The webpage enables users to:
1. Plan hikes with time and weather considerations
2. Engage socially with other hikers
3. View advertisements in designated spaces

Out of scope for this spec: mobile native apps, offline GPS tracking, payment processing (unless advertising requires it — see Section 5).

---

## 2. Functional Requirements

### 2.1 Trip Planning

| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-1.1 | User shall be able to create a new trip plan with a name, date, and destination/trail. |
| FR-1.2 | System shall allow the user to search or select a trail from a database or map interface. |
| FR-1.3 | System shall display estimated hike duration based on trail distance, elevation gain, and a user-selectable pace (e.g., casual/moderate/fast). |
| FR-1.4 | User shall be able to set a planned start time and receive an estimated finish time. |
| FR-1.5 | System shall warn the user if the estimated finish time is after sunset, based on location and date. |
| FR-1.6 | User shall be able to save, edit, and delete trip plans. |
| FR-1.7 | User shall be able to mark a trip plan as "completed" after the fact. |
| FR-1.8 | System shall allow the user to add checklist items (gear, supplies) to a trip plan. |
| FR-1.9 | User shall be able to export or share a trip plan (e.g., link, PDF, or calendar invite). |

### 2.2 Weather Integration

| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-2.1 | System shall retrieve and display a weather forecast for the trail's location on the planned date. |
| FR-2.2 | Weather display shall include temperature range, precipitation probability, wind speed, and sunrise/sunset times. |
| FR-2.3 | System shall issue a visible warning if forecast conditions include severe weather (storms, extreme heat/cold, high wind) on the planned date. |
| FR-2.4 | System shall update the forecast automatically as the trip date approaches (e.g., refresh within 72 hours of the trip). |
| FR-2.5 | If weather data is unavailable for the selected location/date, system shall clearly indicate this rather than showing blank or stale data. |

### 2.3 Time Planning

| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-3.1 | System shall calculate recommended departure time working backward from a desired return time. |
| FR-3.2 | System shall account for daylight hours available on the selected date and location. |
| FR-3.3 | User shall be able to set personal buffer time (e.g., rest stops, photo time) added to base estimates. |
| FR-3.4 | System shall send a reminder notification (email/push, per user preference) a configurable time before the planned start. |

### 2.4 Social Features

| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-4.1 | User shall be able to create a public or private user profile. |
| FR-4.2 | User shall be able to make a trip plan public (invite-only, followers-only, or fully public). |
| FR-4.3 | Other users shall be able to request to join a public trip. |
| FR-4.4 | Trip organizer shall be able to approve/deny join requests. |
| FR-4.5 | Users shall be able to follow other users and see their public completed/upcoming trips in a feed. |
| FR-4.6 | Users shall be able to comment on and react to trip posts (e.g., completed hike write-ups, photos). |
| FR-4.7 | Users shall be able to upload photos to a completed trip. |
| FR-4.8 | System shall provide a direct messaging feature between users. |
| FR-4.9 | System shall provide reporting/blocking functionality for abusive users or content. |
| FR-4.10 | Users shall be able to rate and leave reviews on trails (difficulty, condition, scenery). |
| FR-4.11 | System shall support user groups/clubs for recurring hiking communities. |

### 2.5 Advertising

| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-5.1 | System shall reserve designated, clearly demarcated ad placement zones (e.g., banner, sidebar, native feed placements) distinct from user-generated content. |
| FR-5.2 | Ad content shall be visually distinguishable from organic/user content (e.g., "Sponsored" or "Ad" label). |
| FR-5.3 | System shall support both static image ads and third-party ad network integration (e.g., ad server tags). |
| FR-5.4 | System shall allow targeted ad placement by trail region or activity type, without exposing personally identifiable user data to advertisers without consent. |
| FR-5.5 | System shall support a premium/ad-free subscription tier that suppresses ad placements (optional — confirm with stakeholders whether monetization model includes this). |
| FR-5.6 | Ad load shall not block or delay core page functionality (trip planning, weather data) from loading. |

---

## 3. Non-Functional Requirements

| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| NFR-1 | Weather and trail data shall load within 2 seconds under normal network conditions. |
| NFR-2 | System shall be responsive across desktop, tablet, and mobile browser viewports. |
| NFR-3 | System shall comply with WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility standards. |
| NFR-4 | User data (profiles, messages, location history) shall be encrypted at rest and in transit. |
| NFR-5 | System shall comply with applicable privacy regulations (e.g., GDPR, CCPA) including user data export/deletion requests. |
| NFR-6 | System shall support at minimum the two most recent versions of major browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge). |
| NFR-7 | System shall degrade gracefully if the third-party weather API is unavailable (cached last-known forecast with timestamp, rather than failure). |
| NFR-8 | Ad and tracking scripts shall be isolated (e.g., sandboxed iframes) to prevent them from affecting core site performance or security. |
| NFR-9 | System shall log and monitor uptime, targeting a minimum of 99.5% availability. |

---

## 4. Data Requirements

| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| DR-1 | System shall integrate with a trail database (either licensed third-party data or user-contributed trail records) including distance, elevation profile, and geolocation. |
| DR-2 | System shall integrate with a weather API providing forecast data by geographic coordinates. |
| DR-3 | System shall store user profile data, trip plans, social graph (follows/friends), and content (comments, photos, reviews). |
| DR-4 | System shall maintain an audit trail for moderation actions (reports, blocks, content removal). |

---

## 5. Assumptions & Open Questions

These should be resolved with stakeholders before or during implementation:

- Is there a target advertiser type (outdoor gear brands, tourism boards, local businesses)? This affects ad targeting requirements (FR-5.4).
- Will trail data be sourced from a licensed provider (e.g., AllTrails-style API) or crowdsourced from users?
- Is a paid/premium tier in scope for this version, or a future phase?
- What is the expected initial user base size (affects scalability/NFR targets)?
- Should social features support only individual hikers, or also organizations (hiking clubs, guide companies)?

---

## 6. Acceptance Criteria Format (for downstream use)

Each functional requirement above should be expanded into Given/When/Then acceptance criteria before development begins. Example:

> **FR-2.3** — Severe weather warning
> - Given a trip plan with a saved date and location
> - When the forecast for that date/location includes a weather alert (storm, extreme temperature, high wind threshold)
> - Then the system displays a visible warning banner on the trip plan page before the user can consider the plan "finalized"

