## Problem
Hikers lack reliable offline access to trail info, and groups lose
coordination once connectivity drops on the trail.

## Goals
1. Offline-first trail discovery and navigation.
2. Live group tracking with graceful degradation to check-in messages.
3. Trail condition reports contributed by users (crowdsourced).

## Non-goals (v1)
- Turn-by-turn voice navigation
- Commercial booking/reservations
- Social feed / followers

## Success metrics
- WAU ≥ 25% of installs by month 3
- ≥ 40% of sessions occur with no connectivity
- Condition-report contribution rate ≥ 2% WAU

## Overview
Users can download trail map regions for offline use.

## Functional requirements
- FR-1: User selects a downloadable region by panning/zooming the map
  and tapping "Download this area".
- FR-2: Downloadable area is capped at 500 km² per region; UI shows a
  live km² counter that turns red above 400 km².
- FR-3: Regions are stored encrypted on-device; tiles expire after
  90 days, with a visible "Map data may be stale" banner after expiry.
- FR-4: A region download can be paused, resumed, and cancelled.
- FR-5: Storage usage per region is shown in Downloads list; user can
  delete regions individually.

## Edge cases
- Download interrupted by network loss → resume from last completed
  tile batch; no duplicate work.
- Device storage < 200 MB remaining → block download with clear message.
- App killed mid-download → download auto-resumes on next launch.

## Acceptance criteria (Gherkin)
Feature: Offline map download
  Scenario: Pausing a download
    Given I am downloading the "Mount Rainier NW" region
    When I tap pause
    Then the progress indicator freezes at its current percentage
    And no further tiles are fetched
    When I tap resume
    Then downloading continues from the paused tile batch

  Scenario: Expired offline region
    Given I downloaded a region 91 days ago
    When I open the map with no connectivity
    Then I see the stale-data banner
    And map tiles still render

